`budget.tokens` is 9007199254740993, above 2^53 - 1. Every hash in this contract is taken over canonical bytes, and canonical bytes are RFC 8785, which presumes I-JSON: a number outside the IEEE 754 double range loses precision in some parsers and not others, so two conforming implementations could hash different values from the same text. Every integer field carries `maximum: 9007199254740991` so that can never be the artefact's fault. No real budget comes within six orders of magnitude of it.
